Heather Coppersmith wrote on 07/30/2003 08:11 PM:
> Okay, so I keep getting burdened and then killed, mostly because
> I'm a packrat and can't seem to make good use of my stashes.

My opinion on this:

> When do you make a stash?  Right when you're burdened?  When you
> find "an appropriate place" (whatever that may be)?

Generally one shouldn't stay burdened. If you get burdened and all the
stuff you are carrying seems useful think of making a stash very soon.

If you find an appropriate place and have collected lots of useful
stuff, go ahead an make a stash, even if not burdened. If I haven't
found a bag but have lots of scrolls/potions I would usually make a
stash early on as well--you never know when this gnome with a wand of
fire turns up.

> Where do you make a stash?  In the nearest box or chest?  Near a
> particular dungeon feature?  How far do you drag a chest over to
> that appropriate place?

The deeper the stash the better as you won't have to travel much to
reach it. Altars are a good choice since you tend to return to them for
other reasons and you can always BUC-identify stuff, bless water, etc.

As long as you are only burdened go ahead and move your chest where you
see fit. Controlled levelport, BoH or other methods will come handy for
moving a very heavy stash.

> How do you make a stash?  I know that stacking a boulder on top of
> a box or a chest on top of the E-word is the best, although I
> haven't lost anything I've simply left in a big pile next to the
> stairs, either.

A stash on the stairs is useful for stash-moving and such, but I
wouldn't recommend it for a permament one as you may find yourself on
the stash level through some other means (involuntary levelport,
trapdoors, ...) and be unable to reach it in time to protect it. You
will also wan't to go past that level eventually.

Creatures can pick up stuff that's not in a container. Intelligent ones
will even use it. Some creatures will even pick up a box or--worse--eat
it! That's why a boulder is always nice. And an engraved E-word will
protect it from very large creatures that can lift the boulder. Locking
of boxes is not necessary though.

> Do you make different kinds of stashes for different kinds of
> items?  A box of polypile fodder on one level and a box of water
> just begging to become holy on another?

That's not necessary as containers don't have any storage limit (in my
experience anyway). It may happen that you cannot avoid having divided
stashes, but how you divide the stuff is up to you.

